    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1092">

                <pb facs="1119" n="1105" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/10–3144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-31T16:00:00-06:00">October 31, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>327. Reference Department’s 265, October 30, 9 p.m.<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d1092-f1"/> It became appropriate to clarify Salvador recognition in
                    connection with general discussion with Foreign Minister<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d1092-f2"/> today. The reason for precipitate action here was fact
                    Honduran Government and present Salvadoran Government have a community of
                    interest growing out of developments in Guatemala. Foreign Minister regards
                    present Salvadoran regime as protection to Honduran border<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d1092-f3"/> especially since it is expelling enemies of the
                        Carías<anchor n="43" xml:id="d1092-f4"/> government who have been plotting
                    in San Salvador.</p>
                <p>The Honduran Government considers that the new Salvadoran regime acquired power
                    through constitutional means.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Erwin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1092-f1" n="40" xml:id="d1092-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 37, above.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1092-f2" n="41" xml:id="d1092-f2-content">
                <p>Silverio Laínez.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1092-f3" n="42" xml:id="d1092-f3-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the border dispute between Honduras and Nicaragua, see <ref
                        target="#pg213">pp. 213</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1092-f4" n="43" xml:id="d1092-f4-content">
                <p>Tiburcio Carías Andino, President of Honduras.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
